; Example hledger journal showing the account tree and the conventions
; capabilities/finance expects. Every name here is generic on purpose: the real
; journal lives in the private overlay and this file is published.
;
; Validate with:  hledger --no-conf -f schemas/finance-journal.example check
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The account tree
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
;   assets:bank:<account>              a bank account, named symbolically
;   assets:broker:<broker>:cash        uninvested cash at a broker
;   assets:investments:<broker>:<SYM>  a position, held in its own commodity
;   assets:p2p:<platform>              lending platforms and similar
;   liabilities:card:<issuer>          a credit card
;   income:salary                      employment income
;   income:dividends                   distributions
;   expenses:subscriptions:<slug>      the slug matches the vault note's name
;   expenses:<category>                everything else
;   equity:opening-balances            where a journal starts
;
; Accounts are SYMBOLIC. No IBAN, no account number, no card number, ever, in an
; account name or a comment. Git history is permanent and the knowledge-boundary
; requires that forgetting stay possible; the mapping from a symbolic name to a
; real account lives in Vaultwarden.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Trip attribution
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; A trip expense is also a food expense, so the trip is a posting TAG rather than
; a branch of the tree. Duplicating the category tree under a trip prefix would
; make "what did I spend on food this year" answerable only by remembering to
; union two subtrees.
;
;   hledger -f <journal> balance tag:trip=lisbon-2026
;
; The slug matches the trips capability's plan, which is how the two agree without
; either reading the other's store.

decimal-mark ,
commodity 1.000,00 EUR

account assets:bank:checking
account assets:bank:savings
account assets:broker:cash
account assets:investments:ACME
account expenses:food
account expenses:subscriptions:example-service
account expenses:transport
account income:salary
account equity:opening-balances

2026-01-01 opening balances
    assets:bank:checking                   1.500,00 EUR
    assets:bank:savings                    5.000,00 EUR
    equity:opening-balances

2026-01-31 employer
    assets:bank:checking                   1.200,00 EUR
    income:salary

; A subscription posting. The account slug is the vault note's name, which is how
; observed charges reconcile against what the note claims the price is.
2026-02-01 example service
    expenses:subscriptions:example-service    20,00 EUR
    assets:bank:checking

; Buying a position. The commodity is the ticker, so hledger tracks the share
; count and the cost basis rather than a euro figure that stops meaning anything
; the moment the price moves.
2026-03-14 buy ACME
    assets:investments:ACME                     10 ACME @ 42,50 EUR
    assets:broker:cash

; A market price. pricehist emits these; they are what `-V` and `roi` value a
; position against.
P 2026-08-08 ACME 51,20 EUR

; Trip-tagged spending. Two different categories, one trip, and the tag is what
; joins them.
2026-06-12 dinner  ; trip: lisbon-2026
    expenses:food                             34,80 EUR
    assets:bank:checking

2026-06-12 metro  ; trip: lisbon-2026
    expenses:transport                         6,40 EUR
    assets:bank:checking
